From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:52:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] build: musl cross-build hooks for tokenizers-cpp

When a toolchain file sets LITERTLM_MUSL_HOOK_DIR, add two ExternalProject
steps to tokenizers-cpp_external:
- after patch, delete tokenizers-cpp's hard-coded aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu
  cargo target (it names a nonexistent aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu-gcc);
- between build and install, run 05-tokenizers-c-musl.sh from the hook
  directory, which rebuilds libtokenizers_c.a for <arch>-unknown-linux-musl.
  tokenizers-cpp picks no cargo --target for a generic Linux cross build, so
  its archive is otherwise built for the host glibc triple.
Without LITERTLM_MUSL_HOOK_DIR nothing changes.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
---
 cmake/packages/tokenizers/tokenizers.cmake | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cmake/packages/tokenizers/tokenizers.cmake b/cmake/packages/tokenizers/tokenizers.cmake
index 54af0bce..eca8fd60 100644
--- a/cmake/packages/tokenizers/tokenizers.cmake
+++ b/cmake/packages/tokenizers/tokenizers.cmake
@@ -100,6 +100,27 @@ ExternalProject_Add(
 
 )
 
+# musl cross build: hooks from the directory a toolchain file names in LITERTLM_MUSL_HOOK_DIR.
+if(DEFINED LITERTLM_MUSL_HOOK_DIR)
+  # tokenizers-cpp hard-codes cargo --target aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu (with a nonexistent
+  # aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu-gcc) whenever CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR is aarch64. Drop that line so
+  # it builds for the host triple as it does on x86_64; the rebuild step below retargets it.
+  ExternalProject_Add_Step(tokenizers-cpp_external musl_no_gnu_cargo_target
+    DEPENDEES patch
+    DEPENDERS configure
+    WORKING_DIRECTORY <SOURCE_DIR>
+    COMMAND sed -i /CARGO_TARGET.aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/d CMakeLists.txt
+    COMMENT "[musl] Dropping tokenizers-cpp's aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu cargo target")
+  # tokenizers-cpp passes no cargo --target for a generic Linux cross build, so
+  # libtokenizers_c.a (and the oniguruma the onig crate compiles) comes out for the host glibc
+  # triple and fails to link (undefined __memcpy_chk). Rebuild it for the musl target.
+  ExternalProject_Add_Step(tokenizers-cpp_external musl_rebuild_tokenizers_c
+    DEPENDEES build
+    DEPENDERS install
+    COMMAND "${LITERTLM_MUSL_HOOK_DIR}/05-tokenizers-c-musl.sh" "<SOURCE_DIR>" "<BINARY_DIR>"
+    COMMENT "[musl] Rebuilding libtokenizers_c.a for the musl target")
+endif()
+
 # Do not generate target map for tokenizers-cpp.
 # This project builds internal projects that have not been disabled.
 
